                <head>307. Editorial Note</head>
                <p>From October 23 to 25, Prime Minister Harold Macmillan and other British
                    officials conferred in Washington with President Eisenhower, Secretary Dulles,
                    and other American officials on several matters of mutual concern to their two
                    countries. Documentation on these meetings is scheduled for publication in
                    volume XXVII. Among the matters discussed at these meetings was the exchange of
                    information on nuclear weapons.</p>
            </div>
